  "question": {
    "text": "The figure below shows the top view of a hollow cylindrical room having a frictionless floor. A block of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is projected with a speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>,&nbsp;on the smooth horizontal floor, along the wall of the room. The average normal force exerted by the cylindrical walls, on the block, during its motion from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/3eeede.JPG\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 154px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
